  "dataCard": {},
  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/fisharchive/puntius-sahyadriensis-2/",
      "html": "<p>The Khavlibarb originates from the Yenna River in Satara district in the Indian state of Maharashtra.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/fisharchive/puntius-sahyadriensis-2/",
      "html": "<p>Water conditions are not critical and this species also tolerates a wide range of temperatures.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/fisharchive/puntius-sahyadriensis-2/",
      "html": "<p>The aquarium should be decorated with robust plants and part of the bottom with sandy substrate should be kept open for these fish in order to sift the sand.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/fisharchive/puntius-sahyadriensis-2/",
      "html": "<p>They are omnivorous but need a lot of vegetarian food as well.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/fisharchive/puntius-sahyadriensis-2/",
      "html": "<p>This is a peaceful species, which could however nibble on fresh sprouts of aquarium plants. They can be kept with any peaceful tank mates without any problems.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/fisharchive/puntius-sahyadriensis-2/",
      "html": "<p>There are no reports about breeding yet, but it would probably not be much different from other barb species, i.e. free laying into plants.</p>"
    }
  ],
